      "prompt": "In an isosceles trapezoid $ABCD$, the parallel bases are $AB = 6$ and $CD = 16$, and the non-parallel legs are $AD = BC = 13$. Diagonals $AC$ and $BD$ intersect at point $E$. Find the exact area of triangle $ABE$.",
      "display": "\\text{Trapezoid } ABCD:\\ AB = 6,\\ CD = 16,\\ AD = BC = 13 \\implies \\text{Area}(\\triangle ABE) = ?",
      "plainText": "(1/2) * 6 * sqrt(13^2 - ((16 - 6)/2)^2) * (6/(6 + 16))",
      "answerSpec": {
        "type": "expression",
        "value": "108/11"
      },
      "answerDisplay": "\\frac{108}{11}",
      "answerPlain": "108/11",
      "inputHint": "Enter exact fraction or integer e.g. 35/4 or 42",
      "checkpointHint": "Find trapezoid height $h$ by projecting $AB$ onto $CD$ to get leg base offset $(CD - AB)/2$, then calculate $h = \\sqrt{\\text{leg}^2 - \\text{offset}^2}$. Use similar triangles $\\triangle ABE \\sim \\triangle CDE$ with ratio $AB : CD$ to partition the height.",
      "commonTrapTag": "trapezoid-diagonal-bisect-trap",
      "steps": [
        {
          "latex": "x = \\frac{16 - 6}{2} = 5, \\quad h = \\sqrt{13^2 - 5^2} = \\sqrt{169 - 25} = 12",
          "explain": "Symmetrical base offset gives a right triangle with hypotenuse 13 and base 5."
        },
        {
          "latex": "\\triangle ABE \\sim \\triangle CDE \\implies \\frac{h_1}{h_2} = \\frac{6}{16} = \\frac{3}{8}",
          "explain": "Since $AB \\parallel CD$, alternate interior angles make $\\triangle ABE \\sim \\triangle CDE$."
        },
        {
          "latex": "h_1 = 12 \\times \\frac{3}{3 + 8} = 36/11",
          "explain": "The total height 12 is partitioned in ratio 3:8."
        },
        {
          "latex": "\\text{Area}(\\triangle ABE) = \\frac{1}{2} \\times 6 \\times 36/11 = 108/11",
          "explain": "Calculate area of triangle $ABE$: $\\frac{1}{2} \\times \\text{base} \\times h_1$."
        }
      ],
